{"generated":"2026-11-10T04:22:50.127Z","tz":"America/Los_Angeles","hours":48,"headline":"The wind has weather of its own","lede":"Britannia's skies no longer crawl at one fixed pace: a seeded pressure cycle now drives weather fronts from a becalmed high to a racing gale — and the sea remembers every epoch of it.","notes":[{"tag":"h","text":"BRITANNIA ships variable front speed (PR #1856): each epoch the zonal wind blows becalmed/steady/fresh/gale (0..3 regions), the drift is the cumulative sum — monotone east, deterministic, replay-verifiable. The HUD names the wind when it isn't steady and every shift announces itself."},{"tag":"w","text":"A pixel gate caught a confounder on the way: the heavy-vs-light sea comparison had landed on STORM-vs-CLEAR skies and was measuring the veil, not the wind. Now both sides compare under blue sky — post-front heave vs glass — and the drive is 10/10."},{"tag":"k","text":"PLAICRAFT S1 (#1711) audited end to end: every remaining acceptance line needs Jon's phone and the bound R2 bucket, which defaulted to Hold (#1730). Back on top of the queue as `next` with the exact four-line hardware checklist posted — the moment the bucket exists, a session can close it."},{"tag":"k","text":"Never-dry ladder worked a full lap: queue empty, flagships gap-free, idle.mjs named BRITANNIA weakest (score 6), POLISH issue #1853 filed, claimed, shipped and live inside the time-box."}],"notesFrom":"2026-11-10T04:22:50.127Z","notesCarried":false,"look":[],"strips":[],"stats":{"merged":{"total":3,"builder":2,"qa":1,"ops":0,"slots":{"a":0,"b":0,"both":2,"unknown":0}},"issues":{"closed":9,"opened":7},"overnight":0,"medianMergeMin":12},"rows":[["11-07T21",0,0,0,null,null,null],["11-07T22",0,0,0,null,null,null],["11-07T23",0,0,0,null,null,null],["11-08T00",0,0,0,null,null,null],["11-08T01",0,0,0,null,null,null],["11-08T02",0,0,0,null,null,null],["11-08T03",0,0,0,null,null,null],["11-08T04",0,0,0,null,null,null],["11-08T05",0,0,0,null,null,null],["11-08T06",0,0,